{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:32:20.695Z","ordinal":476,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1570f-a3cd-7de3-9846-8bfc7596f2ee","turn_id":"01a19f3a-6f78-7981-bde5-371fd22f0922","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-32867859-b479-4df2-a2f2-92f9d86aff4b","process_id":"28191","command":["C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\.cache\\codex-runtimes\\codex-primary-runtime\\dependencies\\native\\powershell\\pwsh.exe","-Command","py -3.10 -c \"from audio.youtube import buscar_videos; import json; print(json.dumps(buscar_videos('youtube-dl test video'),ensure_ascii=True))\""],"cwd":"file:///C:/Users/Diego%20Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/Tesis/tesis_karaoke","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"py -3.10 -c \"from audio.youtube import buscar_videos; import json; print(json.dumps(buscar_videos('youtube-dl test video'),ensure_ascii=True))\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"[{\"id\": \"DTi8wZ1a1TA\", \"title\": \"youtube-dl test video [BaW_jenozKc]\", \"channel\": \"yt-dlp Viewers\", \"duration\": 10, \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DTi8wZ1a1TA\"}, {\"id\": \"IMTql0so1yU\", \"title\": \"How to Use Youtube Dl (updated)\", \"channel\": \"The Lone Crater\", \"duration\": 106, \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IMTql0so1yU\"}, {\"id\": \"EJ3gJEDjYgs\", \"title\": \"youtube-dl test (~!@#$%^&*_+{}|\\\":?.;*-=`[]\\\\/'\\\"'\\\",~!@#$%^&*_+{}|\\\":?.;*-=`[]\\\\/'\\\"'\\\",).file\", \"channel\": \"Life Fine\", \"duration\": 6, \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EJ3gJEDjYgs\"}, {\"id\": \"cgYk2Jv0EOU\", \"title\": \"youtube-dl - Downloading Media from Streaming Websites! (Demonstration Test)\", \"channel\": \"TechnoArchivist\", \"duration\": 44, \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cgYk2Jv0EOU\"}, {\"id\": \"75nZ8Vxi7aM\", \"title\": \"Youtube-dl is back!\", \"channel\": \"DenshiVideo\", \"duration\": 194, \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=75nZ8Vxi7aM\"}, {\"id\": \"n3A2q_Ha38A\", \"title\": \"How to use Youtube DL to download channels and playlists pt 2\", \"channel\": \"Frizzle Grustle\", \"duration\": 617, \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n3A2q_Ha38A\"}, {\"id\": \"gr51aVj-mLg\", \"title\": \"Youtube-dl Annotation Test\", \"channel\": \"Jaiz000\", \"duration\": 11, \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gr51aVj-mLg\"}, {\"id\": \"rVklydy1d7A\", \"title\": \"yt-dlp Full Setup & Fix PO Token Error for Windows @Spidy42\", \"channel\": \"Spidy\", \"duration\": 812, \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rVklydy1d7A\"}, {\"id\": \"l7afy7SGZxE\", \"title\": \"The biggest fails from Driving Test | Driving Test 2020\", \"channel\": \"Channel 9\", \"duration\": 640, \"url\": \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7afy7SGZxE\"}]\r\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":3,"nanos":298338500}},"started_at_ms":1793673137397,"completed_at_ms":1793673140695}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:32:21.368Z","ordinal":477,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1570f-a3cd-7de3-9846-8bfc7596f2ee","turn_id":"01a19f3a-6f78-7981-bde5-371fd22f0922","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e9dc5ebd-a689-4567-aadb-5877b3ead802","process_id":"22129","command":["C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\.cache\\codex-runtimes\\codex-primary-runtime\\dependencies\\native\\powershell\\pwsh.exe","-Command","Get-Content ui_live/README.md -TotalCount 100; Get-Content audio/youtube.py"],"cwd":"file:///C:/Users/Diego%20Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/Tesis/tesis_karaoke","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"Get-Content ui_live/README.md -TotalCount 100; Get-Content audio/youtube.py"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Karaoke Studio UI\r\n\r\nInterfaz de escritorio basada en el mockup `Live`, reorganizada en vistas de\r\ntrabajo para separar biblioteca, practica, resultados, historial y ajustes.\r\n\r\n## Abrir\r\n\r\nUsar el lanzador de escritorio:\r\n\r\n```bat\r\niniciar_live.bat\r\n```\r\n\r\nNo abrir `index.html` directamente para una sesion real. Si el archivo se abre en\r\nun navegador normal, no tendra acceso al backend Python, al microfono ni a la\r\nreproduccion con `sounddevice`.\r\n\r\n## Estado actual\r\n\r\n- organiza la aplicacion en vistas: Biblioteca, Practicar, Resultado, Historial y Ajustes\r\n- carga canciones reales desde el catalogo Python\r\n- agrega canciones nuevas desde un selector de audio nativo\r\n- edita titulo y artista sin mover carpetas ni reprocesar audio\r\n- elimina canciones del catalogo con confirmacion\r\n- reprocesa la referencia vocal de la cancion seleccionada\r\n- muestra la curva esperada antes de cantar\r\n- muestra la referencia como bloques grisaceos y colorea el bloque del usuario segun precision\r\n- agrupa los cuadros por nota estable para evitar bloques fantasma en transiciones\r\n- permite ajustar la alineacion visual del usuario para diagnosticar desfases de latencia\r\n- inicia la instrumental y la grabacion con `sounddevice.playrec`\r\n- mide ruido ambiente antes de reproducir para filtrar sonidos de fondo\r\n- recibe puntos de pitch del microfono mediante `pitch_callback`\r\n- descarta saltos extremos en la curva en vivo\r\n- corta el trazo visual cuando hay silencios entre notas\r\n- permite detener y comparar solo el tramo grabado\r\n- muestra el resultado final y el modo detalle\r\n- refresca la curva del usuario cada 120 ms con ventanas de pitch de 0.32 s\r\n- guarda cada grabacion como toma con audio, metricas y datos de grafico\r\n- permite revisar tomas guardadas con previsualizacion de desempeno\r\n- reproduce tomas con voz e instrumental sincronizadas, con mute y volumen por pista\r\n- permite alternar la notacion de notas entre espanol e internacional\r\n\r\n## Pendiente\r\n\r\n- permitir elegir manualmente dispositivos de entrada y salida\r\n- afinar latencia/eco cuando la instrumental salga por parlantes\r\n\"\"\"YouTube search/import isolated from the application's Python/audio environment.\r\n\r\nThe worker runs in .youtube-env (Python 3.11+) and emits JSON lines only.\r\nNo credentials, browser cookies or restricted-content workarounds are used.\r\n\"\"\"\r\nimport json\r\nimport os\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\nimport re\r\nimport shutil\r\nimport subprocess\r\nimport sys\r\nimport threading\r\n\r\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\r\nMAX_SECONDS = 1200\r\nMAX_BYTES = 100 * 1024 * 1024\r\n\r\n\r\ndef validar_id(video_id):\r\n    value = str(video_id or '')\r\n    if not re.fullmatch(r'[A-Za-z0-9_-]{11}', value):\r\n        raise ValueError('Selecciona un resultado válido de YouTube.')\r\n    return value\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _ejecutar(action, value, destination='', progreso_callback=None):\r\n    executable = ROOT / '.youtube-env' / ('Scripts/python.exe' if os.name == 'nt' else 'bin/python')\r\n    if not executable.is_file():\r\n        raise RuntimeError('Falta instalar el componente de YouTube. Ejecuta instalar_youtube.bat.')\r\n    env = os.environ.copy()\r\n    env.pop('PYTHONPATH', None)\r\n    env.pop('PYTHONHOME', None)\r\n    env['PYTHONIOENCODING'] = 'utf-8'\r\n    flags = {'creationflags': subprocess.CREATE_NO_WINDOW} if os.name == 'nt' else {}\r\n    process = subprocess.Popen(\r\n        [str(executable), str(Path(__file__).resolve()), action, value, str(destination)],\r\n        stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, text=True,\r\n        encoding='utf-8', errors='replace', env=env, **flags,\r\n    )\r\n    timed_out = threading.Event()\r\n    def expire():\r\n        timed_out.set()\r\n        process.kill()\r\n    timer = threading.Timer(90 if action == 'search' else 900, expire)\r\n    timer.start()\r\n    result = None\r\n    try:\r\n        for line in process.stdout:\r\n            try:\r\n                event = json.loads(line)\r\n            except ValueError:\r\n                continue\r\n            if 'progress' in event and progreso_callback:\r\n                progreso_callback(event['progress'])\r\n            if 'result' in event:\r\n                result = event['result']\r\n            if 'error' in event:\r\n                raise RuntimeError(event['error'])\r\n        process.wait()\r\n        if timed_out.is_set():\r\n            raise RuntimeError('YouTube tardó demasiado en responder. Intenta nuevamente.')\r\n        if process.returncode or result is None:\r\n            raise RuntimeError('No se pudo completar la operación con YouTube. Revisa tu conexión e intenta nuevamente.')\r\n        return result\r\n    finally:\r\n        timer.cancel()\r\n        if process.poll() is None:\r\n            process.kill()\r\n        process.wait()\r\n        process.stdout.close()\r\n\r\n\r\ndef buscar_videos(query):\r\n    query = str(query or '').strip()\r\n    if not 2 <= len(query) <= 200:\r\n        raise ValueError('Escribe entre 2 y 200 caracteres para buscar una canción.')\r\n    return _ejecutar('search', query)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef descargar_audio(video_id, destination, progreso_callback=None):\r\n    return _ejecutar('download', validar_id(video_id), destination, progreso_callback)\r\n\r\n\r\nclass _Logger:\r\n    def debug(self, message):\r\n        pass\r\n    def warning(self, message):\r\n        pass\r\n    def error(self, message):\r\n        pass\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _options():\r\n    options = dict(quiet=True, no_warnings=True, logger=_Logger(), noplaylist=True,\r\n                   socket_timeout=20, retries=2, extractor_retries=2, cachedir=False)\r\n    node = shutil.which('node')\r\n    if node:\r\n        options['js_runtimes'] = {'node': {'path': node}}\r\n    return options\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _resumen(entry):\r\n    if not entry or not re.fullmatch(r'[A-Za-z0-9_-]{11}', str(entry.get('id', ''))):\r\n        return None\r\n    duration = entry.get('duration')\r\n    if entry.get('live_status') in ('is_live', 'is_upcoming', 'post_live') or entry.get('is_live'):\r\n        return None\r\n    if duration is not None and (duration <= 0 or duration > MAX_SECONDS):\r\n        return None\r\n    return dict(id=entry['id'], title=entry.get('title') or 'Sin título',\r\n                channel=entry.get('channel') or entry.get('uploader') or '',\r\n                duration=duration, url='https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=' + entry['id'])\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _buscar(query, factory):\r\n    options = {**_options(), 'extract_flat': True, 'skip_download': True}\r\n    with factory(options) as ydl:\r\n        info = ydl.extract_info('ytsearch10:' + query, download=False)\r\n    results, seen = [], set()\r\n    for entry in (info or {}).get('entries') or []:\r\n        item = _resumen(entry)\r\n        if item and item['id'] not in seen:\r\n            results.append(item)\r\n            seen.add(item['id'])\r\n    return results\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _descargar(video_id, destination, factory, emit):\r\n    import imageio_ffmpeg\r\n    video_id = validar_id(video_id)\r\n    destination = Path(destination).resolve()\r\n    destination.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\r\n    url = 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=' + video_id\r\n    last_percent = [-1]\r\n    def progress(data):\r\n        downloaded = data.get('downloaded_bytes') or 0\r\n        if downloaded > MAX_BYTES:\r\n            raise ValueError('El audio supera el límite de 100 MB.')\r\n        if data.get('status') == 'downloading':\r\n            total = data.get('total_bytes') or data.get('total_bytes_estimate')\r\n            percent = min(100, int(downloaded * 100 / total)) if total else 0\r\n            if percent != last_percent[0]:\r\n                emit({'progress': f'Descargando audio: {percent}%'})\r\n                last_percent[0] = percent\r\n    options = {**_options(), 'format': 'bestaudio/best', 'max_filesize': MAX_BYTES,\r\n               'outtmpl': str(destination / 'source.%(ext)s'), 'progress_hooks': [progress]}\r\n    with factory(options) as ydl:\r\n        info = ydl.extract_info(url, download=False)\r\n        if not _resumen(info) or not info.get('duration'):\r\n            raise ValueError('Selecciona un video de duración conocida, de hasta 20 minutos y que no esté en directo.')\r\n        emit({'progress': 'Descargando audio…'})\r\n        ydl.process_info(info)\r\n        source = Path(ydl.prepare_filename(info)).resolve()\r\n    if source.parent != destination or not source.is_file():\r\n        raise ValueError('No se obtuvo un archivo de audio completo.')\r\n    if source.stat().st_size > MAX_BYTES:\r\n        raise ValueError('El audio supera el límite de 100 MB.')\r\n    emit({'progress': 'Convirtiendo audio para preparar la canción…'})\r\n    output = destination / 'audio.wav'\r\n    flags = {'creationflags': subprocess.CREATE_NO_WINDOW} if os.name == 'nt' else {}\r\n    subprocess.run([imageio_ffmpeg.get_ffmpeg_exe(), '-nostdin', '-y', '-i', str(source),\r\n                    '-vn', '-ac', '2', '-ar', '44100', '-c:a', 'pcm_s16le', str(output)],\r\n                   stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, check=True, timeout=120, **flags)\r\n    if not output.is_file() or output.stat().st_size <= 44:\r\n        raise ValueError('El audio descargado está vacío.')\r\n    return dict(path=str(output), source=dict(provider='youtube', video_id=video_id,\r\n                url=url, title=info.get('title', ''), channel=info.get('channel') or info.get('uploader', '')))\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _main():\r\n    def emit(event):\r\n        print(json.dumps(event, ensure_ascii=False), flush=True)\r\n    try:\r\n        from yt_dlp import YoutubeDL\r\n        action, value = sys.argv[1:3]\r\n        if action == 'search':\r\n            result = _buscar(value, YoutubeDL)\r\n        elif action == 'download':\r\n            result = _descargar(value, sys.argv[3], YoutubeDL, emit)\r\n        else:\r\n            raise ValueError('Operación no válida.')\r\n        emit({'result': result})\r\n    except ValueError as exc:\r\n        emit({'error': str(exc)})\r\n    except Exception:\r\n        emit({'error': 'No se pudo obtener el contenido de YouTube. Comprueba tu conexión. '\r\n              'El video podría no estar disponible o requerir acceso restringido. '\r\n              'Si persiste, actualiza el componente con instalar_youtube.bat.'})\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == '__main__':\r\n    _main()\r\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":477641400}},"started_at_ms":1793673140890,"completed_at_ms":1793673141367}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:32:21.388Z","ordinal":478,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19f40-1c8c-71e2-969e-1092f3387d27","call_id":"call_21b2f3445a514043bfaf9b7a56bdf295","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"2cf8ed\",\"wall_time_seconds\":3.2984069,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":413,\"output\":\"[{\\\"id\\\": \\\"DTi8wZ1a1TA\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"youtube-dl test video [BaW_jenozKc]\\\", \\\"channel\\\": \\\"yt-dlp Viewers\\\", \\\"duration\\\": 10, \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DTi8wZ1a1TA\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"IMTql0so1yU\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"How to Use Youtube Dl (updated)\\\", \\\"channel\\\": \\\"The Lone Crater\\\", \\\"duration\\\": 106, \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IMTql0so1yU\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"EJ3gJEDjYgs\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"youtube-dl test (~!@#$%^&*_+{}|\\\\\\\":?.;*-=`[]\\\\\\\\/'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\",~!@#$%^&*_+{}|\\\\\\\":?.;*-=`[]\\\\\\\\/'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\",).file\\\", \\\"channel\\\": \\\"Life Fine\\\", \\\"duration\\\": 6, \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EJ3gJEDjYgs\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"cgYk2Jv0EOU\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"youtube-dl - Downloading Media from Streaming Websites! (Demonstration Test)\\\", \\\"channel\\\": \\\"TechnoArchivist\\\", \\\"duration\\\": 44, \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cgYk2Jv0EOU\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"75nZ8Vxi7aM\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Youtube-dl is back!\\\", \\\"channel\\\": \\\"DenshiVideo\\\", \\\"duration\\\": 194, \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=75nZ8Vxi7aM\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"n3A2q_Ha38A\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"How to use Youtube DL to download channels and playlists pt 2\\\", \\\"channel\\\": \\\"Frizzle Grustle\\\", \\\"duration\\\": 617, \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n3A2q_Ha38A\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"gr51aVj-mLg\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"Youtube-dl Annotation Test\\\", \\\"channel\\\": \\\"Jaiz000\\\", \\\"duration\\\": 11, \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gr51aVj-mLg\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"rVklydy1d7A\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"yt-dlp Full Setup & Fix PO Token Error for Windows @Spidy42\\\", \\\"channel\\\": \\\"Spidy\\\", \\\"duration\\\": 812, \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rVklydy1d7A\\\"}, {\\\"id\\\": \\\"l7afy7SGZxE\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"The biggest fails from Driving Test | Driving Test 2020\\\", \\\"channel\\\": \\\"Channel 9\\\", \\\"duration\\\": 640, \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l7afy7SGZxE\\\"}]\\r\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"ae3d6d\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.4778904,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2526,\"output\":\"# Karaoke Studio UI\\r\\n\\r\\nInterfaz de escritorio basada en el mockup `Live`, reorganizada en vistas de\\r\\ntrabajo para separar biblioteca, practica, resultados, historial y ajustes.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Abrir\\r\\n\\r\\nUsar el lanzador de escritorio:\\r\\n\\r\\n```bat\\r\\niniciar_live.bat\\r\\n```\\r\\n\\r\\nNo abrir `index.html` directamente para una sesion real. Si el archivo se abre en\\r\\nun navegador normal, no tendra acceso al backend Python, al microfono ni a la\\r\\nreproduccion con `sounddevice`.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Estado actual\\r\\n\\r\\n- organiza la aplicacion en vistas: Biblioteca, Practicar, Resultado, Historial y Ajustes\\r\\n- carga canciones reales desde el catalogo Python\\r\\n- agrega canciones nuevas desde un selector de audio nativo\\r\\n- edita titulo y artista sin mover carpetas ni reprocesar audio\\r\\n- elimina canciones del catalogo con confirmacion\\r\\n- reprocesa la referencia vocal de la cancion seleccionada\\r\\n- muestra la curva esperada antes de cantar\\r\\n- muestra la referencia como bloques grisaceos y colorea el bloque del usuario segun precision\\r\\n- agrupa los cuadros por nota estable para evitar bloques fantasma en transiciones\\r\\n- permite ajustar la alineacion visual del usuario para diagnosticar desfases de latencia\\r\\n- inicia la instrumental y la grabacion con `sounddevice.playrec`\\r\\n- mide ruido ambiente antes de reproducir para filtrar sonidos de fondo\\r\\n- recibe puntos de pitch del microfono mediante `pitch_callback`\\r\\n- descarta saltos extremos en la curva en vivo\\r\\n- corta el trazo visual cuando hay silencios entre notas\\r\\n- permite detener y comparar solo el tramo grabado\\r\\n- muestra el resultado final y el modo detalle\\r\\n- refresca la curva del usuario cada 120 ms con ventanas de pitch de 0.32 s\\r\\n- guarda cada grabacion como toma con audio, metricas y datos de grafico\\r\\n- permite revisar tomas guardadas con previsualizacion de desempeno\\r\\n- reproduce tomas con voz e instrumental sincronizadas, con mute y volumen por pista\\r\\n- permite alternar la notacion de notas entre espanol e internacional\\r\\n\\r\\n## Pendiente\\r\\n\\r\\n- permitir elegir manualmente dispositivos de entrada y salida\\r\\n- afinar latencia/eco cuando la instrumental salga por parlantes\\r\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"YouTube search/import isolated from the application's Python/audio environment.\\r\\n\\r\\nThe worker runs in .youtube-env (Python 3.11+) and emits JSON lines only.\\r\\nNo credentials, browser cookies or restricted-content workarounds are used.\\r\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\r\\nimport json\\r\\nimport os\\r\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\r\\nimport re\\r\\nimport shutil\\r\\nimport subprocess\\r\\nimport sys\\r\\nimport threading\\r\\n\\r\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\r\\nMAX_SECONDS = 1200\\r\\nMAX_BYTES = 100 * 1024 * 1024\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef validar_id(video_id):\\r\\n    value = str(video_id or '')\\r\\n    if not re.fullmatch(r'[A-Za-z0-9_-]{11}', value):\\r\\n        raise ValueError('Selecciona un resultado válido de YouTube.')\\r\\n    return value\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef _ejecutar(action, value, destination='', progreso_callback=None):\\r\\n    executable = ROOT / '.youtube-env' / ('Scripts/python.exe' if os.name == 'nt' else 'bin/python')\\r\\n    if not executable.is_file():\\r\\n        raise RuntimeError('Falta instalar el componente de YouTube. Ejecuta instalar_youtube.bat.')\\r\\n    env = os.environ.copy()\\r\\n    env.pop('PYTHONPATH', None)\\r\\n    env.pop('PYTHONHOME', None)\\r\\n    env['PYTHONIOENCODING'] = 'utf-8'\\r\\n    flags = {'creationflags': subprocess.CREATE_NO_WINDOW} if os.name == 'nt' else {}\\r\\n    process = subprocess.Popen(\\r\\n        [str(executable), str(Path(__file__).resolve()), action, value, str(destination)],\\r\\n        stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, text=True,\\r\\n        encoding='utf-8', errors='replace', env=env, **flags,\\r\\n    )\\r\\n    timed_out = threading.Event()\\r\\n    def expire():\\r\\n        timed_out.set()\\r\\n        process.kill()\\r\\n    timer = threading.Timer(90 if action == 'search' else 900, expire)\\r\\n    timer.start()\\r\\n    result = None\\r\\n    try:\\r\\n        for line in process.stdout:\\r\\n            try:\\r\\n                event = json.loads(line)\\r\\n            except ValueError:\\r\\n                continue\\r\\n            if 'progress' in event and progreso_callback:\\r\\n                progreso_callback(event['progress'])\\r\\n            if 'result' in event:\\r\\n                result = event['result']\\r\\n            if 'error' in event:\\r\\n                raise RuntimeError(event['error'])\\r\\n        process.wait()\\r\\n        if timed_out.is_set():\\r\\n            raise RuntimeError('YouTube tardó demasiado en responder. Intenta nuevamente.')\\r\\n        if process.returncode or result is None:\\r\\n            raise RuntimeError('No se pudo completar la operación con YouTube. Revisa tu conexión e intenta nuevamente.')\\r\\n        return result\\r\\n    finally:\\r\\n        timer.cancel()\\r\\n        if process.poll() is None:\\r\\n            process.kill()\\r\\n        process.wait()\\r\\n        process.stdout.close()\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef buscar_videos(query):\\r\\n    query = str(query or '').strip()\\r\\n    if not 2 <= len(query) <= 200:\\r\\n        raise ValueError('Escribe entre 2 y 200 caracteres para buscar una canción.')\\r\\n    return _ejecutar('search', query)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef descargar_audio(video_id, destination, progreso_callback=None):\\r\\n    return _ejecutar('download', validar_id(video_id), destination, progreso_callback)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nclass _Logger:\\r\\n    def debug(self, message):\\r\\n        pass\\r\\n    def warning(self, message):\\r\\n        pass\\r\\n    def error(self, message):\\r\\n        pass\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef _options():\\r\\n    options = dict(quiet=True, no_warnings=True, logger=_Logger(), noplaylist=True,\\r\\n                   socket_timeout=20, retries=2, extractor_retries=2, cachedir=False)\\r\\n    node = shutil.which('node')\\r\\n    if node:\\r\\n        options['js_runtimes'] = {'node': {'path': node}}\\r\\n    return options\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef _resumen(entry):\\r\\n    if not entry or not re.fullmatch(r'[A-Za-z0-9_-]{11}', str(entry.get('id', ''))):\\r\\n        return None\\r\\n    duration = entry.get('duration')\\r\\n    if entry.get('live_status') in ('is_live', 'is_upcoming', 'post_live') or entry.get('is_live'):\\r\\n        return None\\r\\n    if duration is not None and (duration <= 0 or duration > MAX_SECONDS):\\r\\n        return None\\r\\n    return dict(id=entry['id'], title=entry.get('title') or 'Sin título',\\r\\n                channel=entry.get('channel') or entry.get('uploader') or '',\\r\\n                duration=duration, url='https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=' + entry['id'])\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef _buscar(query, factory):\\r\\n    options = {**_options(), 'extract_flat': True, 'skip_download': True}\\r\\n    with factory(options) as ydl:\\r\\n        info = ydl.extract_info('ytsearch10:' + query, download=False)\\r\\n    results, seen = [], set()\\r\\n    for entry in (info or {}).get('entries') or []:\\r\\n        item = _resumen(entry)\\r\\n        if item and item['id'] not in seen:\\r\\n            results.append(item)\\r\\n            seen.add(item['id'])\\r\\n    return results\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef _descargar(video_id, destination, factory, emit):\\r\\n    import imageio_ffmpeg\\r\\n    video_id = validar_id(video_id)\\r\\n    destination = Path(destination).resolve()\\r\\n    destination.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\r\\n    url = 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=' + video_id\\r\\n    last_percent = [-1]\\r\\n    def progress(data):\\r\\n        downloaded = data.get('downloaded_bytes') or 0\\r\\n        if downloaded > MAX_BYTES:\\r\\n            raise ValueError('El audio supera el límite de 100 MB.')\\r\\n        if data.get('status') == 'downloading':\\r\\n            total = data.get('total_bytes') or data.get('total_bytes_estimate')\\r\\n            percent = min(100, int(downloaded * 100 / total)) if total else 0\\r\\n            if percent != last_percent[0]:\\r\\n                emit({'progress': f'Descargando audio: {percent}%'})\\r\\n                last_percent[0] = percent\\r\\n    options = {**_options(), 'format': 'bestaudio/best', 'max_filesize': MAX_BYTES,\\r\\n               'outtmpl': str(destination / 'source.%(ext)s'), 'progress_hooks': [progress]}\\r\\n    with factory(options) as ydl:\\r\\n        info = ydl.extract_info(url, download=False)\\r\\n        if not _resumen(info) or not info.get('duration'):\\r\\n            raise ValueError('Selecciona un video de duración conocida, de hasta 20 minutos y que no esté en directo.')\\r\\n        emit({'progress': 'Descargando audio…'})\\r\\n        ydl.process_info(info)\\r\\n        source = Path(ydl.prepare_filename(info)).resolve()\\r\\n    if source.parent != destination or not source.is_file():\\r\\n        raise ValueError('No se obtuvo un archivo de audio completo.')\\r\\n    if source.stat().st_size > MAX_BYTES:\\r\\n        raise ValueError('El audio supera el límite de 100 MB.')\\r\\n    emit({'progress': 'Convirtiendo audio para preparar la canción…'})\\r\\n    output = destination / 'audio.wav'\\r\\n    flags = {'creationflags': subprocess.CREATE_NO_WINDOW} if os.name == 'nt' else {}\\r\\n    subprocess.run([imageio_ffmpeg.get_ffmpeg_exe(), '-nostdin', '-y', '-i', str(source),\\r\\n                    '-vn', '-ac', '2', '-ar', '44100', '-c:a', 'pcm_s16le', str(output)],\\r\\n                   stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, check=True, timeout=120, **flags)\\r\\n    if not output.is_file() or output.stat().st_size <= 44:\\r\\n        raise ValueError('El audio descargado está vacío.')\\r\\n    return dict(path=str(output), source=dict(provider='youtube', video_id=video_id,\\r\\n                url=url, title=info.get('title', ''), channel=info.get('channel') or info.get('uploader', '')))\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\ndef _main():\\r\\n    def emit(event):\\r\\n        print(json.dumps(event, ensure_ascii=False), flush=True)\\r\\n    try:\\r\\n        from yt_dlp import YoutubeDL\\r\\n        action, value = sys.argv[1:3]\\r\\n        if action == 'search':\\r\\n            result = _buscar(value, YoutubeDL)\\r\\n        elif action == 'download':\\r\\n            result = _descargar(value, sys.argv[3], YoutubeDL, emit)\\r\\n        else:\\r\\n            raise ValueError('Operación no válida.')\\r\\n        emit({'result': result})\\r\\n    except ValueError as exc:\\r\\n        emit({'error': str(exc)})\\r\\n    except Exception:\\r\\n        emit({'error': 'No se pudo obtener el contenido de YouTube. Comprueba tu conexión. '\\r\\n              'El video podría no estar disponible o requerir acceso restringido. '\\r\\n              'Si persiste, actualiza el componente con instalar_youtube.bat.'})\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\nif __name__ == '__main__':\\r\\n    _main()\\r\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19f3a-6f78-7981-bde5-371fd22f0922","create_time":1793673141.3886125}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
